# Documented trade-off (RESULTS.md, "Settings that trade durability"), from seed 7 of the
# exploration e5/02-fsync_false. Without the filer's path rule fsync (SeaweedFS's default),
# neither the filer's leveldb2 nor the volume servers sync an acknowledged write, and a power
# cut of the guest before step 1 loses an acknowledged filer PUT. It needs the build
# --set fsync=false; on the default build (fsync=true) hydo repro --regressions skips it.
# found by `hydo explore` (seed 7): durable-defaults
